<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Rhenish Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1923 CE – 1924 CE · capital Koblenz</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Separatist state proclaimed in the occupied Rhineland in 1923 with French backing, which collapsed amid popular hostility.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>During the hyperinflation and the Franco-Belgian occupation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruhr">Ruhr</a> in 1923, Rhenish separatists sought a state independent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a>. In October 1923 armed groups seized town halls in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-aachen">Aachen</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koblenz">Koblenz</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trier">Trier</a> and other towns, and a Rhenish Republic was proclaimed, with a provisional government in Koblenz led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josef-friedrich-matthes">Josef Friedrich Matthes</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hans-adam-dorten">Hans Adam Dorten</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic controlled little beyond public buildings occupied with the tolerance of French and Belgian troops. It had no administration, money or popular support, and its armed bands requisitioned food and goods. In November 1923 local residents fought separatists in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siebengebirge">Siebengebirge</a> near Aegidienberg, and a related separatist government in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/electoral-palatinate">Palatinate</a> was ended by the assassination of its leader in January 1924.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Faced with hostility and British opposition, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> withdrew support, and the movement collapsed by early 1924. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland">Rhineland</a> remained part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> within the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/weimar-republic">Weimar Republic</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/rhenish-republic.jpg" alt="Rhenish Republic" width="320" height="192"><figcaption>Image: Bundesland Nordrhein-Westfalen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_North_Rhine-Westphalia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1923 CE – 1924 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Koblenz</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Josef Friedrich Matthes, Hans Adam Dorten</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Rheinische Republik</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1924&amp;focus=rhenish-republic" aria-label="Rhenish Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4819 416 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Rhenish Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5139 672L5300 622"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5300 622h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5139 672h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5139 672h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1924&amp;focus=rhenish-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
